  "title": "Claudius Ptolemy",
  "summary": "Claudius Ptolemy (c. 85–165 CE) was a Greek astronomer, mathematician and geographer who made observations at Alexandria in Roman Egypt between 127 and 141 CE. His Almagest, known by its Arabic name, set out an Earth-centred model of the heavens in which planets move on epicycles, and his Geography described the known world using latitude and longitude. His geocentric system prevailed for some 1,400 years, until Copernicus put the Sun at the centre in 1543.",
